# configMapGenerator input for `hope-lmstudio-config` (EXECUTION-PLAN §14.4 item 2).
#
# ALMOST EMPTY, ON PURPOSE. It carries exactly ONE key, and that key is a
# bootstrap TRANSPORT ADDRESS — the only category `09-infrastructure-devops.md`
# §Configuration Tiers admits into the `env` tier.
#
# Everything else this workload needs at runtime is either:
#
#   * baked into the IMAGE, because it is a property of the artifact and must
#     not be weakenable from a manifest — HOPE_EXPECT_ACCEL is the load-bearing
#     example (00-project-context.md §Configuration Principles: an engine
#     selection is not a manifest knob), or
#   * set explicitly on the Deployment's container, where it sits next to the
#     comment explaining why (LMS_SERVER_HOST, HOPE_ACCEL_ENFORCE, LMS_LOAD), or
#   * DB-tier config resolved tenant -> SYSTEM through `AiProviderConnection` /
#     `AiTaskDefault`, which is where the base URL, the model selection and any
#     credential belong.
#
# Adding any OTHER key here would move a value OUT of the governed tier and into
# an env var that cannot change without a restart (§Configuration Tiers L1). If
# you find yourself wanting one, check first that it is not really a
# `db-config` / `global-kv` value.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MinIO S3 endpoint for the model-sync Job (ADDED 2026-08-30)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WHY IT BELONGS HERE AND NOT IN A SECRET:
# an endpoint is not a secret. `10.10.1.102:9000` is a LAN address; the thing
# that authenticates is the `hope-models-reader` MinIO service account, which
# stays in a Secret. It previously lived TWICE in the wrong places — as a
# hardcoded literal in `lmstudio.yaml`, and platform-wide as
# `hope-secrets.MINIO_ENDPOINT` (`secrets.dev.yaml.example:55`, still holding the
# PUBLIC tunnel hostname). A stale Secret value fails OPEN onto the public
# internet; a ConfigMap key referenced NON-OPTIONALLY fails the pod instead, and
# is the one form CI's `config-refs` check can validate.
#
# CONSUMED BY: the `hope-lmstudio-model-sync` Job as AWS_ENDPOINT_URL, via a
# NON-OPTIONAL configMapKeyRef. The SERVING pod never reads it — it reads
# weights from the PVC the Job warmed, and never speaks S3.
#
# ⚠️ TRANSPORT: HTTPS, VERIFICATION DISABLED — OWNER DIRECTIVE 2026-08-30.
# The scheme is `https://`. MinIO serves TLS on :9000 and ONE PORT SERVES ONE
# SCHEME, so moving this workload to plain HTTP would have forced pgBackRest,
# GitLab, Loki, Tempo, Prometheus and both cloudflared origins to be re-pointed
# as collateral. The endpoint is therefore unchanged.
#
# What changed is TRUST. The owner directed that the private "ARCAAI Internal
# CA" be removed from this workload ENTIRELY — no ConfigMap, no `SSL_CERT_FILE`,
# no mount — and that AUTHENTICATION be a MinIO SERVICE ACCOUNT (access key +
# secret) and nothing else. Certificate verification is therefore EXPLICITLY
# TURNED OFF at the client: `mc --insecure` on every `mc` invocation in
# lmstudio.yaml's sync Job. `ROOT_CONFIG_REQUEST R-1` (create ConfigMap
# `arcaai-internal-ca`) is CANCELLED by that decision — see ../README.md §3.
#
# ⚠️ THIS IS A DELIBERATE, REVERSIBLE RELAXATION, taken because PHI hardening is
# de-prioritised for now. Recorded so it is trivially findable when PHI matters
# again. What it costs: an unverified TLS connection encrypts the wire but does
# NOT authenticate the peer, so it stops passive capture on 10.10.1.0/24 but not
# an on-path attacker. `hope-lmstudio-model-sync-egress` still confines the
# traffic to a single /32. Model INTEGRITY is unaffected either way — sync.sh
# verifies every file against the prefix's own SHA256SUMS and refuses to write
# the `.ready` sentinel on a mismatch. Only confidentiality and peer
# authenticity are relaxed.
#
# REINSTATEMENT IS TWO EDITS: drop `--insecure` from the `mc` invocations in
# lmstudio.yaml (the `config host add` line AND `mc mirror` inside sync.sh), and
# restore `SSL_CERT_FILE=/etc/ssl/arcaai/ca.crt` plus the `arcaai-ca` ConfigMap
# volume + mount. This line does not change.
LMSTUDIO_S3_ENDPOINT_URL=https://10.10.1.102:9000
